{{also|hon hon hon|Appendix:Variations of "hon"}}
==English==

===Etymology 1===
Shortened from {{m|en|honey}}. 

The transgender slang sense derives from the supposedly abundant use of "hon" as a term of address by older male-to-female transgender people, presumably as a way to verbally affect a femininity they are otherwise perceived by some to lack (due to not [[pass]]ing well), and is especially associated with the cliché phrase "you look great, hon". 

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|hun}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{enPR|hŭn}}, {{IPA|en|/hʌn/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-hon.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌn|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|Hun}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|mostly as a term of address}} {{l|en|honey|Honey}}, [[sweetheart]], {{n-g|a term of endearment}}; {{lb|en|Southern US}}<!--and elsewhere?--> {{n-g|a friendly term of address}}.
#: {{ux|en|Hey, '''hon'''! How was your day at work?}}
# {{lb|en|transgender slang|4chan|derogatory}} A [[trans woman#Noun|trans woman]] who does not [[pass#Verb|pass]]; a [[clocky#Adjective|clocky]] trans woman.
#: {{ant|en|passoid}}
#: {{ux|en|This [[youngshit#Noun|youngshit]] [[mog#Verb|mogs]] me: I'm such a '''hon'''.}}
