#* {{quote-web|en|author=@addamschloe|work=w:Twitter|url=https://twitter.com/addamschloe/status/1016753430310907904|date=10 July 2018|passage=[cw anti-trans slurs] I get that they're rarer than 'trap' (being used to describe trans women as intentional deceivers) but I'd like it if people could be equally hostile to the terms 'brick' and ''''hon'''' honestly<br>it's all transmisic garbage|brackets=on|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220507222940/https://twitter.com/addamschloe/status/1016753430310907904}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=@addamschloe|work=w:Twitter|url=https://twitter.com/addamschloe/status/1016753845723123718|date=10 July 2018|passage='brick' refers to a trans woman who doesn't 'pass', ''''hon'''' refers to a trans woman who doesn't pass and also is nice to other trans women who don't pass, particularly used against older trans women|brackets=on|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210605183723/https://twitter.com/addamschloe/status/1016753845723123718}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=@MsBdUnicorn|work=w:Twitter|url=https://twitter.com/MsBdUnicorn/status/1260213760255557633|date=12 May 2020|passage=Consider the fact that /tttt/ calls any positive trans space a hugbox full of '''hons'''. We're still hung up about passing and it's so pathetic.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230220181143/https://twitter.com/MsBdUnicorn/status/1260213760255557633}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=@stacycay|work=w:Twitter|url=https://twitter.com/stacycay/status/1532239646754758658|date=2 June 2022|passage=listen '''hon''', if you're a "biological boy" that's cool and all but the rest of us are trans women.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221115050727/https://twitter.com/stacycay/status/1532239646754758658}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=@mishawave|work=w:Twitter|url=https://twitter.com/mishawave/status/1570820236244557828|date=16 September 2022|passage=i feel like that depends on how you're using it. referring to yourself as a "'''hon'''", or using it as a joke, sure. but calling other trans people '''hons''' directly or indirectly is a bit far imo. it's an insult about something specific, so it's different from general slurs like "tranny"|brackets=on|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221115220339/https://twitter.com/mishawave/status/1570820236244557828}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=w:Andrea James|title=Transgender slang, slurs, and controversial words|work=Transgender Map|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230408181533/https://www.transgendermap.com/resources/words/slang-slurs/|date=16 April 2019|passage=It [the word "hon"] comes from the cliché, "You look great, '''hon'''," which is often used by older transitioners who do not "pass."}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Natalie Wynn|work=ContraPoints|title=Incels|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fD2briZ6fB0|date=August 17 2018|passage=[24:45] On TTTT, a major piece of jargon is "'''hon'''," a slur used by trans women for other trans women.}}

